# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IS NOT IN THIS REPOSITORY, AND WHY
#
# The working tree is ~4.6 GB. GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB and degrades badly past
# about 1 GB per repository, so the bulk below is excluded. Everything excluded is either
# REGENERABLE from what IS here, or is third-party material that should not be redistributed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Agent working files and rendered page images: 2.5 GB, and every byte is reproducible by
# re-running the pipeline. `steps/*/out/*.json` are the agents' actual ANSWERS and are kept.
data_flow/*/steps/*/work/
data_flow/*/steps/*/tmp/
data_flow/*/steps/*/*.png
data_flow/*/steps/**/*.png

# NCERT source PDFs (766 MB). Copyright NCERT -- not ours to redistribute. The pipeline reads
# them from here; a new clone must supply its own copies at the same paths.
data_flow/*/source_pdfs/

# Question-paper sources and their extractions (1 GB) -- same reasoning: third-party papers.
data_flow/paper_extraction/papers/
data_flow/paper_extraction/steps/
data_flow/ncert_to_paper_maps/steps/

# Cropped figures ARE kept (~130 MB). They are on the CDN as well, but a CDN URL is a
# pointer to someone else's server: if that bucket is cleared or the account changes, the
# artwork is gone and nothing in this repo can rebuild it -- several of these crops exist
# only because an agent measured a region no other tool could find (Figure 1.1's vector
# flowchart, the Ernst Mayr portrait). They are the work product, so they are committed.
data_flow/*/figures_rendered/
data_flow/*/reference_pages/

# Superseded and parked output
data_flow/*/legacy_exports/
data_flow/*/ncert_index/
data_flow/*/_parked/
data_flow/*/x/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Nothing here has ever held a credential -- `upload_assets.py` reads the CDN token
# from the environment and never writes it anywhere -- and these rules keep it that way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
**/cdn.json
**/credentials*.json

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# macOS
.DS_Store
